        "math_academy_id": "q-340308",
        "problem": "If $f(x)=\\frac{tan\u2061x}{x}$,  find ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        "worked_solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=tan\u2061x$ and $v(x)=x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(tan\u2061x)^{\u2032}\\cdot x-tan\u2061x\\cdot (x)^{\u2032}}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sec}^{2}\u2061x\\cdot x-tan\u2061x\\cdot 1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x{sec}^{2}\u2061x-tan\u2061x}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
        "deliberately_incorrect_submission": false,
        "submitted_fields": [
          {
            "key": "field-1",
